From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:35:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/47] Z 6III: a RAW frame owed by a capture tick is delivered
 after group 0 stops

847c7f4 gated raw_pipeline_tick() on the sensor's capture timing
(z63-lv-frame-done: no frame while event_timing_active is false). Live
view's sensor-mode cycle turns 1508 group 0 off right after a capture
tick -- sub_41169F08 -> sub_4116E6A8(0), every other frame while the
meter asks for its long-exposure simulation -- so the frame that tick
owed (z63_raw_owed) reached the gate with the timing already off and was
dropped. Its frame job then never got its completions, and live view
stopped after a few seconds.

The owed count is what pairs a capture tick with its frame; the gate
only repeated it, wrongly, so import_z9lab.py no longer adds it. A tick
still never produces more than it owes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/arm/nikon-z9-pixels.h  |  5 -----
 z63-tools/import_z9lab.py | 12 ------------
 2 files changed, 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hw/arm/nikon-z9-pixels.h b/hw/arm/nikon-z9-pixels.h
index f05ef6f..ee0fab8 100644
--- a/hw/arm/nikon-z9-pixels.h
+++ b/hw/arm/nikon-z9-pixels.h
@@ -133,11 +133,6 @@ static void raw_pipeline_tick(void *opaque)
     if (s->primary_stopped_source_reset_model && !s->event_timing_active) {
         return;
     }
-    /* Z 6III (z63-lv-frame-done, z9lab_attach.c.in): the same gate -- a
-     * frame only while the sensor's capture timing runs. */
-    if (s->raw_pipeline_output_done && !s->event_timing_active) {
-        return;
-    }
     /* 40c26780 selects one of two banks. 40c26790/26824 then write four
      * rows at +200 + bank*200. Original40e9b928 refills the other bank
      * only after C0 bit3, via40e8b0e8. Keep batch ownership until all
diff --git a/z63-tools/import_z9lab.py b/z63-tools/import_z9lab.py
index b4df3eb..f199667 100644
--- a/z63-tools/import_z9lab.py
+++ b/z63-tools/import_z9lab.py
@@ -303,18 +303,6 @@ pedit("""    if (!s->raw_pipeline_model) { return; }
